On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:28:50 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Recent patch series are being produced with new versions, but not
> including the interdiff with previous versions.

You're right. "[PATCH v2 0/7] Add just process-email" [1] and "[PATCH
v3 0/6] Add just process-email" [2] both went out without one. The
cause is that the process-email skill described -v N and the version
notes but never mentioned an interdiff, and format-patch.sh did not
check for one. Whether a revision carried an interdiff depended on my
remembering your request in "Re: [PATCH v3] jails/instances/lab-mail:
Initial spec" [3].

> Review scripts, claude instructions, etc and make whatever changes
> needed to ensure that interdiffs are included with new patch versions.

The fix is posted as "[PATCH 0/2] Require an interdiff on revised
series" [4]:

- libexec/mail/format-patch.sh now refuses -v N for N > 1 unless
  --interdiff is given. A reroll without an interdiff fails before
  anything is formatted, so it cannot reach the list.
- The process-email skill tells the agent to pass --interdiff, and
  shows how to find the previous head: it is the hash leading the
  Message-ID of the last patch of the previous version. The mail
  workflow guide states the same rule.

"[PATCH 0/6] Answer the inbox with lab-process-mail" [5] replaces the
skill with src/lab-process-mail/prompt.md, so whichever series lands
second must carry the Revisions text into prompt.md. The script check
holds either way.

